WEBVTT

00:30.161 --> 00:34.031
(Azure Spring)

00:34.032 --> 00:36.467
(All characters, places, events, etc. depicted are fictional.)

00:36.468 --> 00:38.970
(Children and animals were filmed under strict guidelines.)

00:45.710 --> 00:46.845
Teach me...

00:47.779 --> 00:48.780
how to dive and harvest.

00:59.991 --> 01:00.992
What are you doing?

01:01.726 --> 01:04.329
Are you going to teach me or not?

01:09.668 --> 01:11.469
I don't think I can do that.

01:16.374 --> 01:17.375
Hey!

01:17.709 --> 01:18.877
I can do it, too!

01:19.617 --> 01:21.319
I said, I can do it!

01:25.717 --> 01:27.285
How can he say something like that?

01:27.552 --> 01:28.753
What a punk.

01:34.092 --> 01:40.098
(Episode 2: Troublemaker Cat)

01:58.049 --> 02:00.652
Gosh, that was the worst sleep ever.

02:27.712 --> 02:29.981
Fine. You go and enjoy all your fancy diving...

02:30.415 --> 02:31.816
all by yourself.

02:36.254 --> 02:38.857
What? He didn't go out to dive?

02:41.960 --> 02:42.961
Hey.

02:43.728 --> 02:46.531
You punk... I mean, Mr. Haenam?

02:49.100 --> 02:50.135
Are you around?

02:51.036 --> 02:52.070
Hey.

02:54.673 --> 02:55.674
No?

03:09.020 --> 03:10.956
Darn it. Never mind.

03:33.011 --> 03:34.779
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

03:37.449 --> 03:38.650
Please be here.

03:39.551 --> 03:40.719
Please be here.

03:52.631 --> 03:54.966
I knew it. My mom is the only one...

03:55.901 --> 03:57.035
who's willing to back me up.

04:00.005 --> 04:02.507
You got this, An Na!

04:03.041 --> 04:04.775
- You can do it! - Let's go!

04:04.776 --> 04:06.110
Let's do this!

04:06.111 --> 04:07.378
Let's go!

04:07.379 --> 04:08.479
(Go, Parang-ri Mermaid Seo An Na)

04:08.480 --> 04:10.448
- You can do this! - Good luck!

04:11.616 --> 04:14.252
- You're the best! - Let's go!

04:17.522 --> 04:20.025
- Go! - You got this!

04:22.761 --> 04:24.829
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

04:48.119 --> 04:49.554
Why can't I put this on?

04:50.522 --> 04:51.523
Darn it.

04:52.123 --> 04:53.358
Come on.

05:15.447 --> 05:16.815
- You can do this! - You'll win!

05:17.148 --> 05:18.350
Let's go!

05:18.650 --> 05:20.751
- You can do this! - Let's go!

05:20.752 --> 05:22.787
- Good luck! - Go!

05:23.054 --> 05:24.088
Go get them!

05:24.089 --> 05:25.490
You got this!

05:39.104 --> 05:41.373
You got this, An Na!

05:41.606 --> 05:45.343
- Seo An Na! - You can do it, An Na! Good luck!

05:54.519 --> 05:56.387
(103rd National Swim Meet, 400m)

05:56.388 --> 05:58.356
(7. Seo An Na, Daehan Sports High School)

06:33.458 --> 06:35.093
Ready, go!

06:51.643 --> 06:52.677
To be honest,

06:53.345 --> 06:55.347
it doesn't have to be harvesting seafood.

07:10.028 --> 07:12.631
(Go, Parang-ri Mermaid Seo An Na)

07:21.006 --> 07:22.340
It was to prove that the time...

07:26.011 --> 07:27.479
that stopped for me that day...

07:31.449 --> 07:33.752
could start moving again.

07:46.198 --> 07:48.066
That was all I ever wanted.

08:25.303 --> 08:26.404
Darn it.

08:28.406 --> 08:30.375
An Na... An Na!

08:54.566 --> 08:55.634
Where am I?

08:57.869 --> 08:58.937
The punk from earlier?

08:59.304 --> 09:00.805
I'm not asleep.

09:03.008 --> 09:05.911
What happened?

09:07.712 --> 09:08.813
You're up, so let's go.

09:14.619 --> 09:18.522
Wait, am I allowed to leave just like this?

09:18.523 --> 09:21.626
Of course. You've been asleep for 12 hours.

09:26.131 --> 09:27.799
I see. Thank you.

09:36.741 --> 09:39.010
Hey, did you bring me here?

09:39.277 --> 09:40.679
How did you find me?

09:41.513 --> 09:43.315
Did you pull me out of the water?

09:44.115 --> 09:46.718
Wait, did you pull me out and do mouth-to-mouth...

09:47.152 --> 09:48.253
resuscitation...

09:51.089 --> 09:52.849
Was I supposed to just leave you there then?

09:53.959 --> 09:56.294
Well, that wasn't what I meant.

10:02.167 --> 10:04.302
Hey... Hey!

10:30.262 --> 10:31.542
I should've just left you there.

10:39.171 --> 10:40.405
You've lost your mind, An Na.

10:42.974 --> 10:44.542
You already have a boyfriend...

10:44.543 --> 10:46.077
yet you let another guy kiss you.

10:50.081 --> 10:51.149
No.

10:52.017 --> 10:53.285
I didn't let him do it.

10:53.652 --> 10:55.620
That heinous man was the one who did it.

10:56.821 --> 10:57.856
Yes.

11:05.330 --> 11:06.431
Hey.

11:07.532 --> 11:09.166
I gave this a thought, and...

11:09.167 --> 11:11.803
- Do you eat abalone? - I do. Wait.

11:12.437 --> 11:14.071
What about abalone? That's random.

11:14.072 --> 11:15.740
- How about hijiki? - I do.

11:17.242 --> 11:19.110
I'm trying to talk. Why are you...

11:25.383 --> 11:27.752
Why are you so full of yourself?

11:28.119 --> 11:29.821
I thought the kitchen was a common area.

11:29.988 --> 11:31.556
No, not that.

11:34.125 --> 11:35.805
You mean the mouth-to-mouth resuscitation?

11:37.863 --> 11:39.464
Yes, that.

11:41.933 --> 11:43.368
I mean, sure.

11:43.668 --> 11:45.203
Thank you for saving me,

11:46.505 --> 11:47.639
but I have...

11:49.040 --> 11:50.375
a boyfriend.

11:50.876 --> 11:51.943
So what?

11:53.912 --> 11:57.282
I'm already taken, so you can't just come up to me...

11:57.916 --> 11:59.717
and do that, putting me in a tough spot.

11:59.718 --> 12:00.998
You should've found another way.

12:01.286 --> 12:03.822
- I am looking for another way. - What?

12:04.322 --> 12:07.592
Abalones are good for freedivers, helping the lungs and bronchial tubes.

12:08.393 --> 12:11.496
Hijiki replenishes your minerals and calms your stomach.

12:16.067 --> 12:17.068
By any chance,

12:18.670 --> 12:19.971
are you looking after me?

12:23.475 --> 12:26.043
Otherwise, you'll either steal my food or cause me trouble...

12:26.044 --> 12:27.145
by diving into the sea.

12:29.848 --> 12:31.248
Is that the only way you can speak?

12:53.271 --> 12:54.706
Come to think of it,

12:55.073 --> 12:57.042
my mom always had hijiki and abalones on days...

12:57.843 --> 12:59.811
when the sea was especially rough.

13:01.580 --> 13:03.481
Mom, I'm hungry.

13:04.216 --> 13:05.684
What's for dinner?

13:06.484 --> 13:09.454
I need to eat hijiki and abalones after a rough day out in the sea.

13:09.888 --> 13:11.356
I caught lots of abalones.

13:12.557 --> 13:15.927
Goodness, today was an extra tough day.

13:16.328 --> 13:17.895
Gosh, that sounds delicious.

13:17.896 --> 13:20.165
I almost died back there.

13:24.202 --> 13:25.437
Goodness.

13:46.124 --> 13:48.994
All right. Here.

13:49.528 --> 13:51.596
Freedivers have to sit in the cold sea all day,

13:52.831 --> 13:54.666
swallowing salty water endlessly,

13:56.968 --> 13:59.608
- and hold their breath countless times. - Looks good, doesn't it?

14:00.238 --> 14:02.278
So hijiki and abalone porridge was the best remedy.

14:49.588 --> 14:52.624
This is the best remedy when you fall in and swallow lots of water.

14:53.391 --> 14:55.393
I told you not to call it falling!

14:57.028 --> 15:00.365
Goodness. I'm glad to hear you shout.

15:01.967 --> 15:03.201
Eat up.

15:05.770 --> 15:09.975
It's definitely a little darker than a gold medal.

15:10.175 --> 15:12.176
- Mom. - What?

15:12.177 --> 15:14.312
I like things that are darker.

15:14.946 --> 15:16.982
Look how dark it is. I love it.

15:18.717 --> 15:20.719
All right. Fine. Eat up.

15:27.259 --> 15:28.827
A bite of tender abalone...

15:29.294 --> 15:30.795
slows down my heavy breathing.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.671
And a crunchy piece of hijiki...

15:40.405 --> 15:41.773
calms down my upset stomach.

15:59.925 --> 16:02.327
The most nutritious dish for Parang-ri Mermaids...

16:03.562 --> 16:04.629
melts me completely,

16:06.531 --> 16:07.566
back then...

16:08.466 --> 16:09.634
and even now.

16:13.038 --> 16:14.339
You do your dishes.

16:19.211 --> 16:20.245
Seriously...

16:20.979 --> 16:22.347
Why is he so nice to me?

16:24.749 --> 16:26.251
Are you dating Coach Cha?

16:27.319 --> 16:28.687
What are you talking about?

16:28.954 --> 16:30.422
I have no time to date anyone.

16:31.256 --> 16:33.959
Watch out for guys who are nice to you.

16:34.292 --> 16:36.928
They're the sly ones, not anyone else.

16:42.100 --> 16:44.302
My mom told me to watch out for nice guys.

17:09.160 --> 17:10.729
I'll be careful if I need to,

17:11.863 --> 17:13.265
but I still need to thank him.

17:20.472 --> 17:21.573
Excuse me.

17:24.476 --> 17:25.544
What?

17:26.077 --> 17:27.679
Where does he go every morning?

17:41.593 --> 17:42.627
He's not here, either.

17:44.462 --> 17:47.131
Hello, everyone. Today, I'll sing...

17:47.132 --> 17:49.200
my favourite song, "Oh My," for you.

17:49.201 --> 17:50.267
Two, three.

17:50.268 --> 17:53.872
Oh my, oh my, don't do this.

17:54.239 --> 17:55.774
Women's feelings are.

18:01.980 --> 18:03.514
Why are you glancing around?

18:03.515 --> 18:04.582
Looking for someone?

18:04.583 --> 18:05.650
The punk...

18:05.984 --> 18:08.152
I mean, the freediver who lives at my place.

18:08.153 --> 18:10.188
Oh, you mean Duk Hyun?

18:10.956 --> 18:13.058
Around this hour, he's probably at...

18:14.192 --> 18:16.394
Wait, why are you looking for him?

18:16.661 --> 18:19.430
He made me some porridge,

18:19.431 --> 18:21.099
- but I never got to thank... - Porridge?

18:21.766 --> 18:24.035
He made you porridge?

18:25.770 --> 18:26.771
Did he make it himself?

18:28.840 --> 18:31.376
Darn it. Hey! Yoon Duk Hyun!

18:32.010 --> 18:33.278
Where are you going?

18:34.346 --> 18:36.848
- Hey! - Duk Hyun!

18:37.282 --> 18:38.782
Yoon Duk Hyun!

18:38.783 --> 18:40.986
Where are you going, Su Jeong?

18:44.256 --> 18:45.490
Hey, Su Jeong!

19:11.850 --> 19:13.018
What's going on?

19:13.285 --> 19:15.253
I didn't know he could smile like that.

19:24.162 --> 19:25.197
Duk Hyun.

19:27.699 --> 19:30.068
Did you make porridge for An Na?

19:35.040 --> 19:36.474
I did. What about it?

19:39.211 --> 19:40.312
How could this happen?

19:41.313 --> 19:42.447
Duk Hyun.

19:42.981 --> 19:45.183
I know we're living in a coastal village,

19:47.285 --> 19:50.222
but you can't play with my feelings!

19:51.623 --> 19:52.924
Why, Duk Hyun!

20:11.710 --> 20:14.346
Su Jeong had a misunderstanding.

20:16.548 --> 20:17.682
I don't care.

20:20.185 --> 20:22.020
My goodness.

20:22.587 --> 20:24.489
You're such a punk.

20:30.028 --> 20:31.663
I wasn't talking to you.

20:32.297 --> 20:35.233
These days, cats that act like a little menace...

20:35.500 --> 20:36.701
are called this,

20:37.569 --> 20:39.971
"troublemaker cats."

20:40.772 --> 20:42.474
You came this far to tell me that?

20:50.715 --> 20:51.917
Thank you.

20:55.887 --> 20:56.955
I forgot...

20:57.756 --> 20:59.391
to tell you this yesterday.

21:04.029 --> 21:05.130
It's all right.

21:05.897 --> 21:08.433
I wanted to prevent any future trouble.

21:09.000 --> 21:11.403
I also decided to thank you...

21:12.363 --> 21:14.499
because otherwise, it'll only make me look bad.

21:18.523 --> 21:19.991
Actually, when you said...

21:20.779 --> 21:22.013
you saw many who moved here...

21:23.281 --> 21:26.751
only to resent their failures without committing to anything,

21:29.487 --> 21:30.967
it felt like you were calling me out.

21:31.823 --> 21:32.924
It sounded just like me.

21:36.027 --> 21:37.729
I'm like that.

21:40.999 --> 21:42.801
Swimming is all I've done in my life.

21:44.402 --> 21:45.837
But I've become so broken...

21:46.838 --> 21:48.278
that I can't even fight the current.

21:52.177 --> 21:53.378
My life's pretty much ruined.

21:57.415 --> 21:59.150
That was why I insisted...

21:59.951 --> 22:01.553
that I could be a freediver.

22:05.757 --> 22:07.797
Your life isn't ruined just because you can't swim.

22:11.263 --> 22:13.565
There are tons of people in the world who can't swim.

22:15.934 --> 22:18.169
I was an athlete, and...

22:18.170 --> 22:19.171
But now,

22:20.338 --> 22:22.407
you're just my landlord.

22:23.842 --> 22:25.777
There's no problem even if you can't swim.

22:31.650 --> 22:32.784
And just to let you know,

22:34.753 --> 22:37.622
when I said I couldn't teach you, I was talking about me.

22:39.124 --> 22:40.926
I'm an awful teacher.

22:49.367 --> 22:50.402
Can you...

22:52.103 --> 22:53.271
just try and teach me...

22:54.739 --> 22:55.774
how to harvest seafood?

22:59.277 --> 23:00.378
Both you and I...

23:01.746 --> 23:03.815
might be more talented than we thought.

23:17.162 --> 23:18.663
Start by holding your breath.

23:28.940 --> 23:30.041
Wait for me!

23:48.860 --> 23:49.961
That's so salty!

23:55.200 --> 23:56.902
It's because this is seawater.

23:57.536 --> 24:00.071
I can hold my breath for up to three minutes in a pool.

24:01.339 --> 24:03.008
Do you harvest seafood in a pool?

24:03.475 --> 24:04.476
Again.

24:05.510 --> 24:06.511
Darn it.

24:14.586 --> 24:17.556
Yoon Duk Hyun moved to Parang-ri three years ago...

24:17.989 --> 24:19.491
and began diving.

24:29.167 --> 24:32.370
He heads to the seashore alone whenever the tide is right,

24:32.838 --> 24:36.942
swims through the sea, dives underwater, and harvests seafood.

24:57.829 --> 25:00.031
Abalone, sea squirt,

25:01.166 --> 25:03.235
conch, and octopus.

25:04.302 --> 25:06.671
I watch him harvest these things given by nature.

25:07.739 --> 25:08.807
His life seems peaceful...

25:09.574 --> 25:10.742
and tranquil.

25:13.545 --> 25:15.046
I also want what he has.

25:18.583 --> 25:21.752
But to be honest, my worries tend to melt away...

25:21.753 --> 25:23.255
whenever I eat something delicious.

25:26.291 --> 25:27.492
Hey, there.

25:42.107 --> 25:45.143
Stir-fry some sliced garlic in olive oil.

25:48.280 --> 25:50.148
Then add some freshly caught seafood.

25:51.783 --> 25:53.084
It creates a fascinating flavour.

26:02.494 --> 26:04.329
Lastly, throw in some cooked ramyeon noodles.

26:05.997 --> 26:07.465
You won't find a better medicine.

26:12.370 --> 26:13.405
Come on.

26:14.072 --> 26:15.073
Dig in.

26:34.492 --> 26:35.560
Is it good?

26:55.380 --> 26:56.581
Duk Hyun said...

26:56.982 --> 26:58.483
there's absolutely no problem...

26:59.150 --> 27:00.952
even if I can't swim.

27:06.491 --> 27:07.592
Could that...

27:08.627 --> 27:09.761
be really true?

27:13.899 --> 27:15.633
And now, start skipping.

27:15.634 --> 27:18.403
Left, left, left.

27:22.140 --> 27:23.541
We're going downhill now.

27:23.542 --> 27:24.910
Are you going to stop here?

27:25.143 --> 27:27.212
Now, start skipping again.

27:28.480 --> 27:30.949
Left, left,

27:32.017 --> 27:33.084
left.

27:33.885 --> 27:36.687
- This isn't me trying to prove anything... - Left.

27:36.688 --> 27:38.056
Or throwing a tantrum.

27:39.491 --> 27:40.659
Wait up!

27:56.975 --> 27:58.076
I'm just...

27:59.010 --> 28:00.378
curious...

28:10.155 --> 28:12.424
Could this freediver punk's words be true?

28:15.293 --> 28:17.529
Can I also be like him?

28:18.597 --> 28:20.365
What's the kind of peace...

28:21.166 --> 28:22.334
that he felt?

28:27.472 --> 28:28.673
I won, didn't I?

28:31.042 --> 28:32.722
I saw you lifting your face in the middle.

28:33.078 --> 28:34.179
Again.

28:34.446 --> 28:35.447
Darn it.

28:41.319 --> 28:43.588
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

28:45.156 --> 28:47.091
Lift your legs higher and stride wider!

28:47.092 --> 28:49.594
You're a former athlete! Did you train like this as a swimmer?

28:49.895 --> 28:50.962
Darn it.

28:54.165 --> 28:56.168
Whatever. I'm done.

28:56.968 --> 28:58.069
I'm done!

28:59.538 --> 29:00.672
Again!

29:01.072 --> 29:02.207
One more time.

29:03.542 --> 29:05.177
Do not give up. You can run back home.

29:06.011 --> 29:08.747
After I build up enough stamina to follow him into the sea...

29:10.882 --> 29:12.918
and get used to the salty seawater,

29:15.020 --> 29:16.121
could I...

29:16.588 --> 29:17.956
truly change?

29:34.773 --> 29:37.742
Will I ever be fine...

29:38.510 --> 29:40.478
even if I can't swim?

29:56.695 --> 29:57.896
Today's training is over.

30:00.165 --> 30:01.633
What are we eating today?

30:03.702 --> 30:04.769
We aren't done yet.

30:06.505 --> 30:08.573
What? We aren't done?

30:12.511 --> 30:14.179
It's time to go into the water.

30:42.807 --> 30:43.942
Will I...

30:44.776 --> 30:46.011
ever become...

30:47.345 --> 30:48.413
truly fine?

31:00.559 --> 31:02.594
She must've had a shoulder surgery.

31:08.567 --> 31:10.836
Does it look bad?

31:11.336 --> 31:13.605
It must've been a while since she had surgery,

31:13.939 --> 31:16.708
but I don't think that's why she drowned.

31:18.076 --> 31:21.712
Anyway, she fell asleep due to exhaustion,

31:21.713 --> 31:23.615
so don't worry and leave her here.

31:23.882 --> 31:25.550
All right. Thank you.

31:42.167 --> 31:43.301
Mom.

31:48.206 --> 31:50.041
My shoulder is fully healed.

32:00.385 --> 32:01.586
But...

32:05.690 --> 32:08.126
I don't think I can swim again.

32:15.767 --> 32:17.135
I'm sorry, Mom.
